    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25044" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ischĭădĭcus</span></b> ,
			a, um, = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰσχιαδικός,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>relating to the gout in the hip</i>, <i>ischiadic</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dolores,</span>”
				<i>pains in the hip</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					26, 7, 27, § 42</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">passio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cael.
						Aur. Tard. 5, 1, 26</span></i>
			. — Subst., <i>one who has
				the hip-gout</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 25, 13, 106, § 169</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">28, 2, 4, §
			21</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cael. Aur. Tard. 5, 1, 2
		al.</span></i></div>
